  "slug": "biological-brain-types-006a",
  "summary": "Preprints now move untargeted MS2 and lipidomics annotation beyond whole-spectrum matching toward function and retention-time validation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extracting biological meaning from tandem mass spectra in untargeted metabolomics. ANCHor shifts annotation away from whole-spectrum similarity by exploiting fragment anchors shared among similar spectra. Spec2Function pursues a complementary route, inferring biological functions directly from MS2 spectra using a dual-encoder contrastive model with retrieval-augmented generation. The novelty lies in coupling contrastive spectrum representations with retrieval-augmented generation to link spectra to function rather than to structural identity alone. LipidRT applies retention time coherence to validate and expand lipid annotations in reversed-phase LC-MS lipidomics, adding an independent chromatographic check. MSGFLEX, a proteomics and metaproteomics pipeline, and SynCED, a published update of the Toxin and Toxin Target Database, are heterogeneous relative to this thread and are not modelling advances in metabolite annotation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
